::MCR_U03_L04_Quiz_Q01::
Question ID: MCR_U03_L04_Quiz_Q01
MLA Standard: MLA.MCR.DL.5
Question:
Which response best matches this bivariate data skill: identify a positive association?
{
=A. Use the scatterplot or model feature and explain its meaning in context.#Correct. Bivariate interpretation connects the graph or model feature to the paired numerical data.
~B. Use a bar graph for one category.#A bar graph for one category does not address bivariate numerical data.
~C. Assume the relationship proves causation.#Association alone does not prove cause and effect.
~D. Ignore units and context.#Slope, residuals, and predictions need units and context.
}


